<title>CHILE: Mantos Blancos reports copper output up.</title>
<headline>Mantos Blancos reports copper output up.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Copper production at Chilean mine Mantos Blancos rose 60 percent in the first nine months of the year to 90,817 tonnes metal content from the same period last year, the company said.</p>
<p>Sixty-four percent of production consisted of cathodes and the rest was concentrates, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>The company did not give comparative figures for 1995 or the most recent monthly figures.</p>
<p>--Roger Atwood, Santiago newsroom +56-2-699-5595 x211</p>
</text>
